About the fork
--------------

TapRig turns agent-device into a local-first tool for mobile app automation (CLI, MCP server,
and Node.js SDK for iOS, Android, and the other upstream platforms). The fork removes, in
stages:

- integrations with cloud device providers (BrowserStack, AWS Device Farm, TestMu AI /
  LambdaTest, Limrun) and with the agent-device cloud;
- the update check against the npm registry;
- implicit downloads from the Internet during normal commands;
- the remote daemon mode, unless the owner decides otherwise.

The fork keeps local device automation and the HTTP calls that users write on purpose in
their test scripts (Maestro runScript http.post). agent-device has no telemetry; TapRig adds
none.

Status: migration in progress. Until the rebranding stage (E9), the package, binary,
environment variables, and state directory keep the upstream name `agent-device`.

Plan and records: docs/taprig-implementation-plan.md, docs/taprig-decisions.md,
docs/network-audit.md, docs/upstream-sync.md, docs/HANDOFF.md.

